course: dictionary
lesson: 14879
title: Words that move back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recede means to move back or away, or to go down from a high level. «The floodwater receded after three days.» The water went back down, so the road was dry again.
explain: Recede can also mean to become smaller, weaker or less clear. «Her worries receded when her friend called.» The worries did not vanish at once. They grew weaker and faded into the background.
explain: A receding hairline means hair has stopped growing at the front of the head, so the forehead looks higher. It is the same idea: something moving back from where it was before.
fact: Recede is a verb, so its forms are recedes, receded and receding.
fact: «Recede» means to move back or away, or to go down from a high level.
fact: «Recede» can also mean to become smaller, weaker or less clear.
fact: Floods, tides and glaciers can recede, and so can footsteps or memories in a story.
fact: A receding hairline is hair that has stopped growing at the front of the head.
exercise: «The floodwater receded after three days.» What does receded mean? | Turned into mud | *Went back down | Rose higher and higher | Froze solid
exercise: «As the car drove off, its lights receded into the dark.» What is happening to the lights? | Growing brighter | Stopping suddenly | Turning red | *Moving further away and fading
exercise: Grandad says his hairline is receding. What does this mean? | He has lost all his hair in one day | *Hair has stopped growing at the front of his head | His hair is growing longer at the front | He has a new haircut
test: «Her worries receded when her friend called.» Which word is closest in meaning to receded? | Grew | Arrived | *Faded | Shouted
test: Which word means the opposite of receded? | *Advanced | Shrank | Faded | Retreated
exam: Jayden reads «The tide receded and left rock pools behind.» What did the tide do? | Stopped for good | *Went back out | Turned into rain | Came in fast
